## SoC Engine Stress Test: 64-bit ALU
## v0.1.7 Roadmap: Step 2
## 
## Success Criteria:
## - Define a FullAdder component.
## - Use `for i in 0..63:` to stamp 64 instances.
## - Wire the carry chain using dynamic nets.
## - Zero P12 (Collision) or P41 (Disconnected) errors.

import * from @std/primitives/units
import Silicon_P from @std/materials/doped_semiconductors
import Copper from @std/materials/conductors

## 1. Define FullAdder component
component FullAdder:
    pins: [a, b, carry_in, sum, carry_out]
    
    layout:
        shape: Rectangle(8mm, 4mm, 0.5mm)
        pin_positions:
            a at [1mm, 1mm]
            b at [3mm, 1mm]
            carry_in at [5mm, 1mm]
            sum at [1mm, 3mm]
            carry_out at [5mm, 3mm]
    
    metadata:
        component_type: "1-bit Full Adder"
        description: "Standard full adder cell for large-scale arithmetic units."

module SoC_ALU_64_Module:
    pins: []

## 2. The SoC Space
space SoC_ALU_64 implements SoC_ALU_64_Module:
    dimensions: 700mm by 20mm by 4mm
    grid: 700 by 20 by 4
    origin: bl by b
    
    ## Base substrate
    add substrate(Silicon_P) spanning [x:0mm, y:0mm, z:0mm] to [x:700mm, y:20mm, z:1.5mm]
    
    ## 3. Parametric Unroller (64-bit instantiation)
    ## 4. Carry chain wiring using dynamic nets
    for i in 0..63:
        add FullAdder named Adder[i] at [x: 5mm + i * 10mm, y: 5mm, z: 1.5mm]:
            net: [
                a: A[i], 
                b: B[i], 
                carry_in: Carry[i], 
                sum: Sum[i], 
                carry_out: Carry[i+1]
            ]

    ## Validation check: "If hwc build exits with code 0, the silicon is mathematically perfect."
    ## This test verifies the unroller, net binding, and spatial placement of 320 pins.
